ESPF codebooks — vendored from MolTrans
=======================================

These files are the ESPF (Explainable Substructure Partition Fingerprint)
codebooks used by SpinoML's `kind:"espf"` manifest branches to tokenize SMILES
(and protein sequences) into interpretable substructure subword tokens.

Source : https://github.com/kexinhuang12345/MolTrans  (ESPF/ directory)
Method : Huang, Xiao, Hoang, Glass, Sun. "MolTrans: Molecular Interaction
         Transformer for drug–target interaction prediction." Bioinformatics 2021.
         ESPF: Huang, Xiao, Glass, Sun. "Explainable Substructure Partition
         Fingerprint for Protein, Drug, and More." NeurIPS LMRL 2019.

Files
-----
  drug_codes_chembl.txt          subword-nmt BPE merge rules (drug/SMILES, ChEMBL)
  subword_units_map_chembl.csv   subword → index map (drug/SMILES)
  protein_codes_uniprot.txt      subword-nmt BPE merge rules (protein, UniProt)
  subword_units_map_uniprot.csv  subword → index map (protein)

